1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:05,850
Imagine you are changing a pillowcase, and your hand touches something hard inside it.

2
00:00:05,940 --> 00:00:13,930
You open it... and find knotted threads, strands of hair, and a folded paper with writing that can’t be read.

3
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:22,880
Your heart trembles as you remember the past months: arguments for no reason, sleeplessness, and a heart that found no rest in this house.

4
00:00:22,970 --> 00:00:27,420
And the first question that jumps to your mind: who did this?

5
00:00:28,540 --> 00:00:33,010
Before you answer, let’s see what the Qur’an and Sunnah say about sorcery,

6
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:37,070
what signs practitioners mention, and why they are not conclusive,

7
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:43,250
what you should do if you find something like this, and most importantly, what you must not do.

8
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:47,100
Sorcery is real... but it has no independent power.

9
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:54,280
Allah says of those who learn sorcery: “They learn from them what separates a man from his wife,”

10
00:00:54,370 --> 00:01:00,260
and right after: “But they cannot harm anyone with it except by Allah’s permission.”

11
00:01:00,350 --> 00:01:08,890
Keep these two sentences together: sorcery exists, but the sorcerer is no god, and no knot or talisman works except by Allah’s permission.

12
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:12,890
And He says: “And the sorcerer will not succeed wherever he comes.”

13
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:15,040
Signs practitioners mention

14
00:01:15,130 --> 00:01:19,160
Experienced practitioners mention signs that may appear in a house affected by sorcery:

15
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:27,660
sudden aversion and quarrels between spouses, especially if they get along outside the house, but tension starts once they enter it,

16
00:01:27,750 --> 00:01:33,050
heaviness and tightness in the chest on entering the house, and relief on leaving it,

17
00:01:33,140 --> 00:01:41,300
recurring nightmares for more than one family member, and a strange heaviness and slackness toward prayer and Qur’an inside the house,

18
00:01:41,390 --> 00:01:51,050
and the appearance of strange things: knots and hair, papers with symbols and unintelligible writing, or objects no one knows the source of.

19
00:01:51,140 --> 00:01:53,850
And here is the most important point of this episode:

20
00:01:53,940 --> 00:01:58,460
none of these signs alone is conclusive proof of sorcery.

21
00:01:58,550 --> 00:02:05,600
A quarrel between spouses may come from a sharp tongue, too many demands, hardship, or fatigue,

22
00:02:05,690 --> 00:02:09,330
and slackness in worship may come from sins and heedlessness,

23
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:13,580
and many of these situations have clear natural causes.

24
00:02:13,670 --> 00:02:19,880
Allah says: “Whatever misfortune befalls you is because of what your hands have earned, and He pardons much.”

25
00:02:19,970 --> 00:02:26,260
The most dangerous thing is to hang every problem on sorcery and excuse ourselves from responsibility.

26
00:02:26,350 --> 00:02:33,100
If the house is empty of prayer and remembrance, and its people’s tongues are sharp, that is the first thing to fix.

27
00:02:33,190 --> 00:02:39,940
The good news is that the cure for sorcery and the cure for these problems is one path: returning to Allah.

28
00:02:40,030 --> 00:02:42,160
And don’t ask: who did it?

29
00:02:42,250 --> 00:02:46,880
In Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī, the Prophet (peace be upon him) himself was affected by sorcery;

30
00:02:46,970 --> 00:02:55,720
a man called Labīd ibn al-Aʿṣam bewitched him with a comb and hair hidden in a well, and Allah revealed it to him and cured him.

31
00:02:55,810 --> 00:03:01,310
ʿĀʾisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: “O Messenger of Allah, why not take it out and expose it?”

32
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:09,290
He said: “Allah has cured me, and I disliked stirring up evil among people because of it,” and he ordered the well to be filled in.

33
00:03:09,380 --> 00:03:18,440
Reflect: the Prophet (peace be upon him) knew the sorcerer personally, yet he did not want to stir up strife among people.

34
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:24,850
So how can we cut off a sister-in-law, a mother-in-law, a neighbour or a relative over mere suspicion?

35
00:03:24,940 --> 00:03:32,390
Allah says: “O you who believe, avoid much suspicion; indeed some suspicion is sin.”

36
00:03:32,950 --> 00:03:39,090
And know that one of the charlatans’ biggest tricks is to say: “One of your relatives did this to you.”

37
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:46,350
With that one sentence families fall apart, and the charlatan works a sorcery greater than all those knots.

38
00:03:46,950 --> 00:03:49,270
So if you find something, what should you do?

39
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:55,660
First: don’t be afraid; that paper and that thread have no power except by Allah’s permission.

40
00:03:55,750 --> 00:04:04,890
Second: recite al-Falaq, an-Nās and Āyat al-Kursī over it, for Allah taught us to seek refuge in Him “from the evil of those who blow on knots.”

41
00:04:04,980 --> 00:04:15,520
Third: recite the verses that nullify sorcery, such as: “What you have brought is sorcery; Allah will surely nullify it. Allah does not set right the work of corrupters.”

42
00:04:15,610 --> 00:04:20,020
Fourth: untie the knots and put it in water until the writing dissolves,

43
00:04:20,110 --> 00:04:25,880
then get rid of it or bury it, just as the Prophet (peace be upon him) ordered the well to be filled in.

44
00:04:25,970 --> 00:04:30,140
Fifth: don’t show it to anyone who will turn it into gossip and strife.

45
00:04:30,230 --> 00:04:37,270
And never undo sorcery with sorcery; some people, on finding such a thing, go to someone who claims to undo it.

46
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:43,950
The Prophet (peace be upon him) was asked about an-nushra, undoing sorcery with similar sorcery, and he said: “It is the work of the devil.”

47
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:49,410
And he said: “Whoever goes to a fortune-teller and asks him about something, his prayer is not accepted for forty nights.”

48
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:59,570
If anyone asks for your mother’s name, an animal of a particular description to slaughter, gives you a talisman and obscure writing, or asks for a fortune, know that he is a charlatan.

49
00:04:59,660 --> 00:05:02,580
As for protecting and treating the home in the lawful way:

50
00:05:02,670 --> 00:05:07,400
First: Sūrat al-Baqara. He (peace be upon him) said: “Recite Sūrat al-Baqara,

51
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:12,600
for taking it is a blessing, leaving it is a regret, and the sorcerers cannot withstand it,” and al-baṭala means sorcerers.

52
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:16,250
and he told us the devil flees from a house in which Sūrat al-Baqara is recited,

53
00:05:16,350 --> 00:05:20,800
so recite it in your home, even over several days, or share it among the household.

54
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:27,700
Second: the morning and evening adhkār: Āyat al-Kursī, the end of al-Baqara, and al-Ikhlāṣ, al-Falaq and an-Nās three times,

55
00:05:27,700 --> 00:05:32,600
and with them this dhikr a hundred times a day, for it is a protection from the devil until evening:

56
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:37,800
“There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; His is the dominion and His the praise, and He is capable of all things.”

57
00:05:37,890 --> 00:05:47,790
Third: ruqyah water: recite al-Fātiḥa, Āyat al-Kursī, the Muʿawwidhāt and the verses that nullify sorcery over water, and let the household drink from it and wash with it,

58
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:50,400
and many scholars have permitted this.

59
00:05:50,490 --> 00:05:52,530
Fourth: ʿajwa dates.

60
00:05:52,620 --> 00:06:00,970
He (peace be upon him) said: “Whoever eats seven ʿajwa dates every morning, no poison or sorcery will harm him that day.”

61
00:06:01,060 --> 00:06:09,000
Fifth: praying at home. He (peace be upon him) said: “Make some of your prayers in your houses, and do not turn them into graves.”

62
00:06:09,090 --> 00:06:13,150
A house in which people prostrate to Allah is no comfortable place for the devil.

63
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:17,400
Sixth: patience and certainty, for the cure is not completed in a day,

64
00:06:17,490 --> 00:06:20,550
and always remember: “Allah will surely nullify it.”

65
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:25,790
Keep these words: sorcery is real, but it harms only by Allah’s permission.

66
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:30,090
Not every sign is sorcery, and don’t hang every problem on it.

67
00:06:30,180 --> 00:06:35,990
Don’t accuse anyone on suspicion; the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not even expose the sorcerer.

68
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:41,180
Don’t undo sorcery with sorcery, and protect your home with Qur’an, remembrance and prayer.

69
00:06:41,270 --> 00:06:46,570
Send this clip to every family living in fear and suspicion, and write in the comments:

70
00:06:46,660 --> 00:06:50,820
“O Allah, fill our homes with the Qur’an, and fill them with tranquillity and mercy.”

71
00:06:50,910 --> 00:06:51,820
Amen.

